WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.550 align:start position:0%
 
ah  Final Fantasy 15 has been in development  for nearly a decade and as a result has  undergone a multitude of changes but  among these changes what has transformed  the most is the combat system first  available to us in Episode two skaia  combat has changed in a myriad of ways  throughout the various builds here are  all the major ways comet has evolved  episode Disgaea gave us her first taste  of Final Fantasy 15s combat offering a  glimpse at noctis's multi-blade fighting  style this early iteration focused on  equipping weapons to particular  instances of a combo for example you  could assign a spear to the opening blow  of noctis's combo and then assign a  sword to the flurry of attacks that  followed depending on the weapons you  assigned to those particular instances  you could change noctis's fighting style  in interesting ways  while this combat system was subtly  altered with minor balance adjustments  via the episode - sky a 2.0 patch it was  completely overhauled in the Platinum  demo in that build noctis brandished  multiple weapons each with their own  particular set of attacks and animations  and he could manually switch between  them mid combo the combat system in this  build is the same as the final preview  build of the game such as switching the  lock-on button and altering the  armatures attack animations  weapons functions similarly across all  builds with each type retaining its  overall feel and attack animations  however slight alterations were made as  the builds went on episode disguise 2.0  patch added the ability to perform  variations to a weapons attacks  depending on the direction you were  holding for example if you held forward  you can perform lunge attacks with your  sword  the final preview build implements these  changes while adding in enemy  resistances which makes enemies  invulnerable against certain weapon  types but weak against others however a  major feature that didn't make it to the  later builds was the techniques from  episode Disgaea which were powerful  special attacks tied to weapons in your  arsenal that consumed MP  magic wasn't implemented in episode  Disgaea but we did see it in the  Platinum demo where it was showcased as  limited items you could equip and cast  against enemies while this has been  retained in the final preview build  Magic has been made more complex thanks  to the spell crafting system which  allows it to be given special effects  depending on the items you combine it  with in the crafting process for example  you can craft a lightning spell with a  curse status effect that diminishes  enemy attack power in each file fantasy  15 build mana points are tied directly  to noctis's warp blade abilities and  evasive maneuvers in episode Disgaea  evasive maneuvers techniques and  armature consumed MP however when the  2.0 patch was released the game was  updated to exclude guarding right before  an enemy attack from consuming MP these  changes were mostly retained in both the  Platinum demo and the final preview bill  with the exception of Armiger which was  given its own separate meter using too  much MP renders and Octus into a  weakened state called stasis the only  way to recover from this is by taking  cover or warping to a safe space this  constraint has been kept consistent  across all builds though small changes  have been made to balance it initially  in episode Disgaea you could attack in  stasis and you even recovered MP 4 in an  unlimited amount of time when hanging on  to a point orb however you can no longer  do either in both the Platinum demo and  the final preview build  in the initial version of episode  Disgaea you could only defend yourself  by getting it to a stance that allowed  you to face through oncoming enemy  attacks at the cost of MP a much  requested dodge roll was later added in  the 2.0 patch while slight adjustments  were made to how much MP was consumed  when phasing through attacks in the  defensive stance  as you fight enemies in battle your  attacks inevitably stagger them in  episode Ischia this weakened state was  referred to as off-guard however it has  been renamed to vulnerable in the final  preview build a backstab mechanic called  blind site has also been added to the  final preview build this gives you the  ability to deal more damage to enemies  when you hit them from the rear when  episode Disgaea first launched noctis's  party would only support him with  standard attacks however once the 2.0  update rolled around you could perform  cross chains special cooperative attacks  that could only be performed once an  enemy was staggered cooperative attacks  have been updated in the final preview  bill to allow noctus to trigger them  manually each move can be leveled up the  more you use it increasing its overall  effectiveness in battle and there's  plenty more to unlock for each member in  your party the further along you get the  final preview built also adds in link  strike and blindside link these are  special cooperative attacks that only  occur under specific conditions when  you're near an ally link strike occurs  just after a parry while blindside link  occurs when you're behind an enemy and  those are all the major ways combat has  evolved over the years for more and  everything final fantasy 15  stay tuned to games

